            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Msteph"
            },
            "reviewBody": "this was awesome. i didn't have a whip attachment for the food processor, but the regular puree attachment worked great. it's not all light and airy, but the consistency is really nice and firm. it tasted almost like chocolate mousse and not too sweet either.",
            "datePublished": "2011-12-16T06:26:17.203Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used this recipe but substituted 3 tablespoons powdered sugar for the regular sugar and used double chocolate cookie crumbs for the cocoa powder ... about 1/3rd of a cup of crumbs and it tastes delicious.I know it's simple, but it's a winner all around. It even keeps in the refrigerator for 2 days without falling apart.",
            "datePublished": "2011-06-04T15:42:39.170Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "luv2cook"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made it exactly as written, but doubled. It's the perfect frosting for my chocolate raspberry cake. The family loved it. I especially loved how quick and easy it is to put together. I recommend that you chill the cake, along with the mixing bowl and beaters.",
            "datePublished": "2012-01-29T13:33:20.370Z"
          },
          {
